course: dictionary
lesson: 12016
title: The word chiefly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Chiefly is a slightly formal word. You will meet it more in books and science texts than in chat, where people say mainly or mostly. It means mainly or mostly. «Pandas eat chiefly bamboo.» Pandas sometimes eat other things, but bamboo is most of their food. Check it by swapping in mainly: the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Chiefly can also mean above all, or more than anything else. «The trip was chiefly about learning, not games.» The clue is in the words more than games: the main reason for the trip was learning. Here chiefly tells you what matters most.
explain: When you see chiefly, look for the main point in the sentence. It often tells you what is most important, or what most of something is made of.
fact: Chiefly means mainly or mostly.
fact: Chiefly can also mean above all, more than anything else.
fact: Chiefly is a slightly formal word; everyday speech often says mainly or mostly.
fact: «Pandas eat chiefly bamboo» means pandas eat mostly bamboo.
fact: A good check is to swap in mainly and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The team is chiefly made of volunteers.» What does chiefly mean here? | *Mainly | Not at all | Last of all | Quietly
exercise: «We chiefly want to find a way home, not to play.» What does chiefly suggest? | Only a little | Very loudly | Sometimes | *Above all, more than anything else
exercise: Which word could replace chiefly in «The shop sells chiefly fruit»? | Rarely | *Mostly | Sadly | Quickly
test: «Our dog eats chiefly dog biscuits.» What does chiefly mean? | *Mostly | Very fast | Hardly ever | In a loud voice
test: Ruby says chiefly is posh, just say mainly. Why might an author use chiefly? | It means the opposite of mainly | It is a shorter word | *It is a little more formal, and it means much the same as mainly | It means very loud
exam: Which is the best meaning of chiefly in «We ate chiefly soup, with a little bread.»? | Hardly ever | Slowly | *Mostly | Happily
